# Project Instructions — claude_researcher

This file is uploaded to your claude.ai Project. The agent reads it at the start of every session to learn how to reach your GitHub repos.

## Why this uses the GitHub REST API

claude.ai's sandbox has restricted network egress. Standard `git clone` and `git push` won't reach `github.com` over SSH or HTTPS. To make the sandbox able to read and write the user's GitHub repos, network access to `api.github.com` (and a few related domains) was permitted during bootstrap at:

> **Settings → Capabilities → Allow Network Egress → Domain Allow List**

This is a user-wide setting (configured once, applies across all your claude.ai chats — not per-Project). The exact domains configured are recorded in `<USERNAME>/basic_config/domain_allowlist.txt` for reference and for re-use on a different machine.

So instead of cloning the repo, the agent uses GitHub's [Contents API](https://docs.github.com/en/rest/repos/contents) to read and write files via the curl recipes below. (Reads of public upstream content — like skill specs at `raw.githubusercontent.com/danparshall/claude_researcher` — go through claude.ai's built-in WebFetch tool, which doesn't require allow-list configuration. Those don't need recipes here.)

## Credentials

Set these once per session, before any REST call:

```bash
TOKEN="<TOKEN>"
USERNAME="<USERNAME>"
REPO="<REPO>"
```

`<TOKEN>` is the fine-grained GitHub PAT created during bootstrap, scoped to read `<USERNAME>/basic_config` and read/write `<USERNAME>/<REPO>`. `<REPO>` is just the repo name (not `owner/repo`) — the curl recipes below combine it with `<USERNAME>`. Do not commit these values anywhere.

## Reading a file

```bash
curl -s -H "Authorization: token $TOKEN" \
  -H "Accept: application/vnd.github+json" \
  -H "X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2022-11-28" \
  "https://api.github.com/repos/$USERNAME/$REPO/contents/PATH" \
  | python3 -c "import sys,json,base64; print(base64.b64decode(json.load(sys.stdin)['content']).decode())"
```

## Writing a new file

```bash
CONTENT=$(base64 -w0 /path/to/local/file)
curl -s -X PUT -H "Authorization: token $TOKEN" \
  -H "Accept: application/vnd.github+json" \
  -H "X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2022-11-28" \
  "https://api.github.com/repos/$USERNAME/$REPO/contents/PATH" \
  -d "{\"message\":\"commit msg\",\"committer\":{\"name\":\"$USERNAME\",\"email\":\"$USERNAME@users.noreply.github.com\"},\"content\":\"$CONTENT\"}"
```

## Updating an existing file (requires the file's sha)

```bash
SHA=$(curl -s -H "Authorization: token $TOKEN" \
  -H "Accept: application/vnd.github+json" \
  -H "X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2022-11-28" \
  "https://api.github.com/repos/$USERNAME/$REPO/contents/PATH" \
  | python3 -c "import sys,json; print(json.load(sys.stdin)['sha'])")
curl -s -X PUT -H "Authorization: token $TOKEN" \
  -H "Accept: application/vnd.github+json" \
  -H "X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2022-11-28" \
  "https://api.github.com/repos/$USERNAME/$REPO/contents/PATH" \
  -d "{\"message\":\"commit msg\",\"committer\":{\"name\":\"$USERNAME\",\"email\":\"$USERNAME@users.noreply.github.com\"},\"content\":\"$CONTENT\",\"sha\":\"$SHA\"}"
```

## Listing a directory

```bash
curl -s -H "Authorization: token $TOKEN" \
  -H "Accept: application/vnd.github+json" \
  -H "X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2022-11-28" \
  "https://api.github.com/repos/$USERNAME/$REPO/contents/PATH"
```

## Where to start every session

1. Fetch this Project's runtime instructions from upstream:
   `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/danparshall/claude_researcher/main/template/CLAUDE.md`
2. Follow CLAUDE.md's session-start sequence — it tells you which other files to read in what order, and which skills are available.

If anything in this file looks inconsistent with the user's actual setup (wrong username, wrong repo, expired token), stop and surface the mismatch before doing any work.
